doc:article-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "7 The State Party where the alleged offender is prosecuted shall in accordance" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "with its laws communicate the final outcome of the proceedings to the Secretary-General of the United Nations, who shall transmit the information to the other States concerned and the international intergovernmental organizations concerned." ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 1."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-8 ;
    values:originalText "The State Party in the territory of which the alleged offender is found shall, if it does not extradite him, be obliged, without exception whatsoever and whether or not the offence was committed in its territory, to submit the case to its competent authorities for the purpose of prosecution, through proceedings in accordance with the laws of that State. Those authorities shall take their decision in the same manner as in the case of any ordinary offence of a grave nature under the law of that State.  International Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages  Schedule  Crimes (Hostages) Act 1989 Compilation date: 10/3/16 Registered: 25/5/16  2. Any person regarding whom proceedings are being carried out in connexion with any of the offences set forth in article 1 shall be guaranteed fair treatment at all stages of the proceedings, including enjoyment of all the rights and guarantees provided by the law of the State in the territory of which he is present." ;
    skos:definition "The State Party in the territory of which the alleged offender is found shall, if it does not extradite him, be obliged, without exception whatsoever and whether or not the offence was committed in its territory, to submit the case to its competent authorities for the purpose of prosecution, through proceedings in accordance with the laws of that State. Those authorities shall take their decision in the same manner as in the case of any ordinary offence of a grave nature under the law of that State.  International Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages  Schedule  Crimes (Hostages) Act 1989 Compilation date: 10/3/16 Registered: 25/5/16  2. Any person regarding whom proceedings are being carried out in connexion with any of the offences set forth in article 1 shall be guaranteed fair treatment at all stages of the proceedings, including enjoyment of all the rights and guarantees provided by the law of the State in the territory of which he is present."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c3bc16045db341e734d3b6cccf984b9419ca582b64584602a2f545c510f5c481" ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The State Party must submit the case to its competent authorities for prosecution." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
