concept:crimes-hostages-act-1989-article-18 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18 Schedule  International Convention Against The Taking Of Hostages"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-18 ;
    values:originalText "Crimes (Hostages) Act 1989  Compilation date: 10/3/16 Registered: 25/5/16  1. This Convention shall enter into force on the thirtieth day following the date of deposit of the twenty-second instrument of ratification or accession with the Secretary-General of the United Nations. 2. For each State ratifying or acceding to the Convention after the deposit of the twenty-second instrument of ratification or accession, the Convention shall enter into force on the thirtieth day after deposit by such State of its instrument of ratification or accession." ;
    skos:definition "Crimes (Hostages) Act 1989  Compilation date: 10/3/16 Registered: 25/5/16  1. This Convention shall enter into force on the thirtieth day following the date of deposit of the twenty-second instrument of ratification or accession with the Secretary-General of the United Nations. 2. For each State ratifying or acceding to the Convention after the deposit of the twenty-second instrument of ratification or accession, the Convention shall enter into force on the thirtieth day after deposit by such State of its instrument of ratification or accession."@en ;
